From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anxelok <anxelok@localhost>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 12:02:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Trim region bookkeeping from the lease claim path

Every parallel bucket claims and releases an ownership lease each
tick, and each claim paid an exact-lease scan, an overlap set
allocation, a containing-region scan, a region descriptor allocation
with two timestamps, and reference-count maintenance - all feeding
only the aggregate counters in the /loom snapshot. A claim now does
the conflict check, which is the safety contract, and the
registration itself; each lease counts as its own region for the
snapshot's created and retired totals.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/threading/RegionRuntime.java b/net/minecraft/server/threading/RegionRuntime.java
index 50fa9abae92ac9275c3041913dda16f8e6371b96..fdcbc63f30326f981703a36edec7c06e639f7193 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/threading/RegionRuntime.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/threading/RegionRuntime.java
@@ -238,8 +238,6 @@ public class RegionRuntime {
         // lock that claim/release use. Keyed by the Thread object, not the thread id, so the lookup does
         // not box a Long per query. Mutated only while holding `lock`.
         private final ConcurrentHashMap<Thread, Lease[]> leasesByThread = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
-        private final Map<Long, RegionDescriptor> regions = new HashMap<>();
-        private final Map<Long, Integer> regionReferenceCounts = new HashMap<>();
         private long createdRegions;
         private long splitEvents;
         private long mergeEvents;
@@ -260,44 +258,25 @@ public class RegionRuntime {
             try {
